IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tcpss-customer`
IMPORT `tcpss-csg-standard`

-- Telecommunications (Customer Service Guarantee) Standard 2023 -- worked cases, from the phone customer's seat. Expected
-- values were worked by hand from the deposited Standard (Compilation No. 1, F2026C00929), Schedules 1 and 2, never copied from
-- the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Connection periods (s 11, Schedule 1). A flat in Perth (urban centre over 10 000), near a pillar with spare capacity.
#ASSERT `My guaranteed connection period in business days` `an urban centre of 10 000 people or more` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 5
-- The previous tenant's line can be reactivated: 2.
#ASSERT `My guaranteed connection period in business days` `an urban centre of 10 000 people or more` TRUE TRUE EQUALS 2
-- A town of 5 000: 10.
#ASSERT `My guaranteed connection period in business days` `an urban centre or community of more than 2 500 but fewer than 10 000 people` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 10
-- A town of 800: 15. A station homestead: 15.
#ASSERT `My guaranteed connection period in business days` `an urban centre, locality or community of more than 200 but no more than 2 500 people` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `My guaranteed connection period in business days` `somewhere else (200 people or fewer, or no recognised community)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 15
-- No facility nearby with capacity: within 20 business days, wherever the site (s 11(2)).
#ASSERT `My guaranteed connection period in business days` `an urban centre of 10 000 people or more` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 20

-- Repair periods (ss 14, 15).
#ASSERT `My guaranteed repair period in full business days` `an urban centre of 10 000 people or more` FALSE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `My guaranteed repair period in full business days` `an urban centre, locality or community of more than 200 but no more than 2 500 people` FALSE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `My guaranteed repair period in full business days` `somewhere else (200 people or fewer, or no recognised community)` FALSE EQUALS 3
-- The same remote farm, but the fault can be fixed at the exchange without a visit: 1 (s 15).
#ASSERT `My guaranteed repair period in full business days` `somewhere else (200 people or fewer, or no recognised community)` TRUE EQUALS 1

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Damages (Schedule 2). Inputs: what, customer, two or more features, guaranteed period, arranged period, business days
-- taken, excuse.
-- A Perth household's new line, period 5, connected on business day 13: 8 days late. 5 x $14.52 + 3 x $48.40 = $217.80.
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `my phone service was connected late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 5 0 13 `nothing` EQUALS `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` 8 217.80
-- A shop's fault, period 1, fixed on business day 4: 3 days late at $24.20 = $72.60.
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `a fault in my phone service was repaired late` `a business customer` FALSE 1 0 4 `nothing` EQUALS `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` 3 72.60
-- One call-handling feature, residential, 7 days late: 5 x $7.26 + 2 x $24.20 = $84.70.
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `call waiting, forwarding, barring, number display or display blocking was connected or repaired late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 5 0 12 `nothing` EQUALS `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` 7 84.70
-- Two features, business, 6 days late: 5 x $24.20 + 1 x $48.40 = $169.40.
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `call waiting, forwarding, barring, number display or display blocking was connected or repaired late` `a business customer` TRUE 5 0 11 `nothing` EQUALS `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` 6 169.40
-- Connected on day 5 of 5: no contravention.
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `my phone service was connected late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 5 0 5 `nothing` EQUALS `no contravention: the work was done within the period allowed`
-- The household asked for connection after its move, by day 10; connected on day 9: within the arrangement (ss 12(2)(a), item 101(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `my phone service was connected late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 5 10 9 `nothing` EQUALS `no contravention: the work was done within the period allowed`
-- An interim mobile service at fixed-line rates for the whole delay: no delay counted (item 101(2)).
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `my phone service was connected late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 5 0 13 `it supplied me an interim service for the whole delay` EQUALS `no contravention: the provider is excused or exempt (ss 10, 21-24, 31, Schedule 2 item 101(2))`
-- Storm damage, statement given in time: exempt (s 24). Statement never given: the exemption is taken never to have applied (s 25(2)).
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `a fault in my phone service was repaired late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 1 0 4 `circumstances beyond its control, and it gave me the s 26 statement or published the s 27 notice in time` EQUALS `no contravention: the provider is excused or exempt (ss 10, 21-24, 31, Schedule 2 item 101(2))`
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `a fault in my phone service was repaired late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 1 0 4 `circumstances beyond its control, but it gave neither the s 26 statement nor the s 27 notice in time` EQUALS `the provider was late by this many business days, and the scale sets this many dollars` 3 43.56
-- A business with 6 lines: exempt (s 21).
#ASSERT `Did my provider break the guarantee` `a fault in my phone service was repaired late` `a business customer` FALSE 1 0 4 `it supplies me more than 5 eligible telephone services` EQUALS `no contravention: the provider is excused or exempt (ss 10, 21-24, 31, Schedule 2 item 101(2))`

-- The amount owed, through the Act's s 116(2)-(3): $217.80 less a $50 credit already given = $167.80; excused: 0.
#ASSERT `How much guarantee damages must my provider pay under the scale` `my phone service was connected late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 5 0 13 `nothing` 50 EQUALS `answered` 167.80
#ASSERT `How much guarantee damages must my provider pay under the scale` `my phone service was connected late` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` FALSE 5 0 13 `it supplied me an interim service for the whole delay` 0 EQUALS `answered` 0

-- Liability through the Act's s 116(1).
#ASSERT `Am I owed guarantee damages under the Standard` TRUE FALSE FALSE `my phone service was connected late` 5 0 13 `nothing` EQUALS `yes: my provider is liable to pay me damages for the contravention (s 116(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I owed guarantee damages under the Standard` TRUE FALSE FALSE `my phone service was connected late` 5 0 5 `nothing` EQUALS `no: my provider has not contravened a performance standard in relation to me`
#ASSERT `Am I owed guarantee damages under the Standard` TRUE TRUE FALSE `my phone service was connected late` 5 0 13 `nothing` EQUALS `no: I validly waived the customer service guarantee for this service (s 120(2))`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Missed appointments (ss 19, 20, item 205).
#ASSERT `What does the scale set for my missed appointment` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` `for a particular time` 20 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 14.52
#ASSERT `What does the scale set for my missed appointment` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` `for a particular time` 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What does the scale set for my missed appointment` `a business customer` `for a window of up to 4 hours` 999 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 24.20
#ASSERT `What does the scale set for my missed appointment` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` `for a window of more than 4 and up to 5 hours` 10 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 14.52
#ASSERT `What does the scale set for my missed appointment` `a residential customer, or a charitable or welfare organisation` `for a window of more than 4 and up to 5 hours, at a small or remote site the technician had to travel far to reach` 40 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What does the scale set for my missed appointment` `a business customer` `for a particular time` 999 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What does the scale set for my missed appointment` `a business customer` `for a particular time` 999 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0

-- Waivers (ss 33, 34).
#ASSERT `When does my waiver take effect` `in writing` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it takes effect on the day I consented (s 34(8)(a))`
#ASSERT `When does my waiver take effect` `orally` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it takes effect 5 business days after I consented, unless I withdraw my consent before then; the provider must give me a written statement within 3 business days (s 34(7), (8)(b))`
#ASSERT `When does my waiver take effect` `orally` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it has no effect: I withdrew my consent within the 5 business days (s 34(8)(b))`
#ASSERT `When does my waiver take effect` `in writing` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it is not a valid waiver: the provider did not do what s 34(3) or (4) requires`
#ASSERT `When does my waiver take effect` `in writing` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I cannot waive the guarantee for a universal service phone line (s 120(7), s 33)`

-- Which Standard (s 39).
#ASSERT `Which Standard decides my claim` (Date 1 8 2023) EQUALS `the 2011 Standard (s 39), which is not deposited: this module's periods and amounts do not apply`
#ASSERT `Which Standard decides my claim` (Date 1 9 2023) EQUALS `the 2023 Standard, encoded here`

-- The duties as rules (business days). Connected on day 4 of 5: fulfilled. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `the connection duty` 5 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `connect the service` AT 4
-- Repaired on day 4 of 1: breach (s 14(5)). Expected: BREACH.
#TRACE `the repair duty` 1 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `rectify the fault` AT 4
-- Oral waiver statement on day 2: fulfilled. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `the oral waiver statement duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `give me a written statement of the oral waiver` AT 2
